      "title": "What Medicare is",
      "narration": "Dennis turns 65 in March. Medicare is the federal health program for people 65 and older, people under 65 who have received Social Security disability benefits for 24 months, and people with end-stage renal disease or ALS. It is administered by the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services. Part A, hospital insurance, is financed by the payroll tax and is premium-free for people with 40 quarters of covered work. Part B, medical insurance, is financed by premiums and general revenue. Parts A and B together are Original Medicare. Part C is Medicare Advantage and Part D is drug coverage, covered in Lesson 43.",
