      "title": "Enrollment periods",
      "narration": "Dennis’s initial enrollment period is seven months: the three months before his birthday month, the month itself and the three months after. If he already receives Social Security he is enrolled automatically; otherwise he applies. If he misses it, the general enrollment period runs January 1 to March 31 each year, with coverage starting the month after he signs up. If he keeps working with employer coverage from an employer of 20 or more, he may delay Part B without penalty and use an eight-month special enrollment period after the employment or coverage ends. Late Part B enrollment carries a permanent penalty of 10 percent for each full year of delay.",
