      "title": "Part A: hospital insurance",
      "narration": "Part A covers inpatient hospital care, skilled nursing facility care after a qualifying three-day inpatient stay, home health care, hospice and blood after the first three pints. Costs are organized by benefit period, which begins at admission and ends when the patient has been out of the hospital or skilled facility for 60 consecutive days. Each benefit period carries a deductible, 1,736 dollars in 2026. Days one through sixty are then covered in full; days 61 through 90 require a daily coinsurance; and 60 lifetime reserve days with a higher coinsurance can be used once. Skilled nursing care is covered in full for days one through twenty, with coinsurance for days 21 through 100 and nothing after day 100.",
