      "title": "Claims terminology",
      "narration": "When Dennis sees a doctor, the approved amount is what Medicare allows for the service. A provider who accepts assignment agrees to take the approved amount as full payment, bills Medicare directly and collects only the deductible and 20 percent from Dennis. A participating provider accepts assignment for all patients. A nonparticipating provider may refuse assignment and charge up to 15 percent above the approved amount, the limiting charge, which Dennis pays as an excess charge. Providers who opt out of Medicare entirely bill privately under contract. Dennis receives a Medicare Summary Notice showing what was billed, approved and paid, and an advance beneficiary notice warns him before a service Medicare may not cover.",
